You can't directly set the Execution Context Selector via the console, but you can achieve similar functionality through several methods. Here are the ways to control execution context programmatically:

## 1. **Using `debugger` Statement with Context**

```javascript
// This will pause execution in the current context
debugger;

// You can also use conditional debugging
if (condition) {
    debugger;
}
```

## 2. **Accessing Different Contexts via Console**

```javascript
// Access global scope
window.someVariable

// Access iframe contexts
document.querySelector('iframe').contentWindow.someVariable

// Access specific elements' contexts
$0.someProperty  // $0 is the last selected element
```

## 3. **Using Console Utilities for Context Selection**

```javascript
// Switch to different frames
// In console, you can use:
frames[0].someFunction()  // First iframe
frames[1].someFunction()  // Second iframe

// Or access by name
window.frames['frameName'].someFunction()
```

